  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"106\" data-end=\"305\"><strong data-start=\"106\" data-end=\"118\">Hepcidin</strong> is a liver-produced peptide hormone that plays a <strong data-start=\"168\" data-end=\"204\">central role in iron homeostasis</strong>. It regulates iron absorption from the intestine and iron release from macrophages and liver stores.</p>\n<p data-start=\"307\" data-end=\"336\">🩺 <strong data-start=\"310\" data-end=\"336\">Clinical Significance:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"337\" data-end=\"631\">\n<li data-start=\"337\" data-end=\"484\">\n<p data-start=\"339\" data-end=\"484\">Useful in evaluating <strong data-start=\"360\" data-end=\"389\">iron metabolism disorders</strong>, including <strong data-start=\"401\" data-end=\"430\">anemia of chronic disease</strong>, <strong data-start=\"432\" data-end=\"458\">iron deficiency anemia</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"464\" data-end=\"483\">hemochromatosis</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"485\" data-end=\"560\">\n<p data-start=\"487\" data-end=\"560\">Helps differentiate between types of anemia and iron overload conditions.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"561\" data-end=\"631\">\n<p data-start=\"563\" data-end=\"631\">Can be used in <strong data-start=\"578\" data-end=\"605\">monitoring iron therapy</strong> or response to treatment.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Elevated Hepcidin Levels May Indicate</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Anemia of chronic disease</strong> &ndash; Inflammation causes increased hepcidin, limiting iron availability.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Iron overload conditions</strong> &ndash; Such as hereditary hemochromatosis (in some stages).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Chronic infections or inflammatory states</strong> &ndash; IL-6 stimulation leads to hepcidin rise.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Certain malignancies</strong> &ndash; Especially those with systemic inflammation.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
